Package: a-nas-host
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: A-NAS <zhongwater123@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: acl, btrfs-progs, parted, smartmontools, samba, iproute2, udev, systemd, python3, ffmpeg, heif-thumbnailer, libheif-plugin-libde265, libegl1, libgles2, libgomp1, libssl3t64
Suggests: caddy, docker-ce, docker-compose-plugin, tini, socat, ripgrep
Description: what an A-NAS device needs from Debian
 The Host Agent, the Product Service and their workers run these commands
 and link these libraries. The A-NAS installer requires this package at the
 version of the release it installs (docs/adr/0031). Caddy (the LAN entry),
 Docker (the App Center) and the assistant's sandbox tools are suggested:
 each is turned on by its own runbook.
